  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/taint4/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Re-checked at dev 100b6fbb6e: _build_sanitizer_index_multi (taint.py:3538) on aes_gcm::Aes256Gcm::encrypt yields keys {full, 'encrypt'} only (dotted names get Owner.short); short_name (taint.py:460-474) is the hand-rolled split. Wider than filed: the rust analyzer never puts Aes256Gcm::encrypt in the name slot; c.encrypt() and Aes256Gcm::encrypt(c,..) both arrive as rust:aes_gcm::Aes256Gcm:0-0:encrypt, and the module-slot branch builds fq 'aes_gcm::Aes256Gcm.encrypt' -> NO MATCH. The rust rows now live in encryption_community.yaml. MECHANISM: rust :: owner/member split hand-rolled in TaintSanitizer.short_name and the module-slot branch joins module+callee with '.', so rust receiver evidence never matches a '::' catalogue name. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-totob."  # b302
